{"audit": {"coverageKind": "skeleton", "state": "unaudited"}, "axis": "root", "citesSource": "1817d_cuvier", "editorial": {"basis": "Cuvier first used \"Échinodermes\" as an Order in 1798, but treated it as a Class in the 1817 1st Edition of Le Règne Animal. Unlike Hisinger 1837, there does not appear to be a list of cited works, but given that the 1837 paper cites the 1829 2nd Edition, it seems likely that the 1st Edition rather than the 1798 work is intended.\n", "inferred": ["authority"]}, "form": "taxon", "id": "1828_hisinger:0:usage", "kind": "usage", "path": "0", "printed": {"citedAs": "Echinodermata Cuvier"}, "source": "1828_hisinger", "spelling": "echinodermata", "subject": "echinodermata", "tree": "taxonomy"}
