{"audit": {"coverageKind": "skeleton", "state": "unaudited"}, "axis": "children", "form": "taxon", "id": "1828_hisinger:0/children/0:usage", "kind": "usage", "notes": "Order inclusion assumed based on class assignment, although the\norder Pédicellés is not mentioned in the text in any language.\nList of families/genera-taking-the-place-of-families included based on\nHisinger's text, in the following order, which matches Cuvier —\nAsterias, Euryale, Comatula, Encriniterna or Crinoiderna, Echiniterna.\nHe notably uses the genus rather than family Asterias and omits\nOphiura, uses different (non-latin) family names in place of the genus\nEncrinus, uses a distinct (non-latin) spelling of Echinus at family\nrank, and omits the genus Holothuria.  The entire order to the family\nlevel, plus the mentioned asterian genera, is given here for context\ndue to the explicit citation at the class level.\n\"The Sphæronites\" sometimes seem to be discussed as a family, but\nmostly as a genus.  However, the mention of Echino-Encrinites grouped\nwith the genus Sphærohites imples some sort of family, so this\nfollows Cuvier's approach of just using the type genus as the family\nname (e.g. Asterias and Echinus).  As far as I can tell, such a\nfamily-level declaration is not generally attributed to Hisinger,\nbut it is the best I can do with such vague prose.\nEchino-Encrinites is place after Sphæronites simply because it\nseems of secondary concern to Hisinger, as there is no formal list.\n", "path": "0/children/0", "printedAttribution": "as-record", "source": "1828_hisinger", "spelling": "pédicellés-order", "subject": "pédicellés-order", "tree": "taxonomy"}
